# tier, then the glob. The glob is the rest of the line and may contain spaces.
# Do not put a comment after the glob.
# Each changed path gets its own tier. A path that matches nothing is medium.
# The pull request tier is the highest tier among those paths.
# When one path matches more than one glob, the highest tier wins.
# low < medium < high
# Matching is case-insensitive. Paths are not lowercased first.
# scripts/risk-tier.mjs also forces these to high: **/AGENTS.md **/CLAUDE.md
# **/REVIEW.md **/GEMINI.md **/.mcp.json **/.cursorrules **/.cursor/**
# **/.claude/** .github/**

high **/AGENTS.md
high **/CLAUDE.md
high **/REVIEW.md
high **/GEMINI.md
high .cursor/**
high **/.cursor/**
high .claude/**
high **/.claude/**
high **/.mcp.json
high **/.cursorrules
high .github/**
high astro.config.mjs
high lighthouserc.json
high package.json
high package-lock.json
high risk-tiers
high scripts/risk-tier.mjs
high scripts/risk-tier.test.mjs
high .env
high .env.*
high **/.env
high **/.env.*
high **/.dev.vars
high **/.dev.vars.*
high wrangler.toml
high wrangler.json
high wrangler.jsonc
high _headers
high _redirects
high public/_headers
high public/_redirects
high src/content/drafts/**

medium src/pages/**
medium src/styles/**
medium src/components/**
medium src/layouts/**
medium functions/**

low docs/**
low README.md
low src/content/posts/**
low src/content/resume.md
